{
  "_": [
    "aerosmith (the Pro) on Allknowing2012's 'Aerosmith (Original 2021)' 1.01, a scripted",
    "original on the GOTG 2.x framework: vpxshadow.py keeps its script as a shadow game and",
    "hands the ball to the real game. The Pro, not the LE: the table has two flippers and",
    "no upper playfield (the LE's U/P flipper, U/P targets, center drop and control gate),",
    "and its sw63 is the Pro's RIGHT RAMP EXIT. The author named his switches by Stern's",
    "manual numbers (swNN = switch_list's `num` NN), so every switch below is matched by",
    "NAME: sw1 LEFT OUTLANE ... sw63 RIGHT RAMP EXIT; the kickers by place and by what",
    "their subs do (ScoopEject = LEFT SCOOP, ElevatorEject = TOP SCOOP, sw61 = RIGHT EJECT,",
    "ToyBoxKicker = the toy box). Ids: the RIG's switch_list.txt for aerosmith; coils",
    "through group_node.txt (group 6 = node 8, group 7 = node 9).",
    "PinUP: the table's DMDMode 2 path needs PinUP Player and its pack (PuPInit reads",
    "puplayer.getroot, which a PadNoPuP stub cannot answer), so `neuter` takes out its",
    "`elseIf DMDMode = 2` line: the table runs its own no-DMD path (Set PuPlayer = New",
    "PinupNULL, bUsePUPDMD False) on every machine; the rig's LCD and sound are the show.",
    "Lamps: the inserts by what the script does with them (ModeNames order, the",
    "ClearShotMultiplier arrow/X pairs, each AEROSMITH target's own letter) and the rest",
    "by place; GUESS = wants a look at the machine. quiet_subs: its light shows and its",
    "flipper lane-change (RotateLaneLights*), which the machine does itself."
  ],
